  identity: "a_kernel_function_name_realized_for_one_overload_only" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one kernel function name carries two meanings the type checker and the interpreter both accept -- `contains(xs: List<T>, x: T)` as list membership and `contains(s: String, sub: String)` as substring -- while the Rust emission routes every call to the one bridge extdeps.languages.rust.emit rt_functions binds for the name (`contains` -> v1_rt::contains(s: String, sub: String)). HARM: a source the seed accepts and interprets correctly emits Rust that rustc refuses (E0308), so the defect surfaces as an emitted-crate build failure far from its cause, and only for the first native closure that happens to reach the list overload. It is gunbc.design_argument::single_authority's meaning fork at the realization layer: one name, two contracts, one realized.",
    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#15834 (converged ingress M2a, 2026-11-05): gunbc.http_ingress http_ingress_native_argv_from wrote `!contains(declared, a.name)` over a List<String>; the //gunbc/instruments:native-serve build refused it at the emitted gunbc_http_ingress.rs (`v1_rt::contains(declared.clone(), a.name.clone())`, mismatched types). The interpreted http_ingress_witness had passed. That line now reads membership as a filter count, annotated with this row; the emitter is unchanged.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the call type-checks and interprets; the emitted call names the right bridge for the OTHER overload. Read the bridge's Rust signature beside the call's argument types; a String-argument control emits and builds, a List-argument case does not.",
    "FOUND AT MITIGATABLE (the emitted build refuses, loudly, but late). CEILING: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED -- which overload a call means is decided by its resolved argument types, which the emitter already holds. NEXT TRIGGER: the Rust emission selects a kernel function's realization by the call's resolved argument types (or the kernel declares the two meanings under two names), SUFFICIENT FOR a List membership `contains` in an emitted closure to build and the String one to build unchanged; until then a native-closure author writes membership as a filter count and cites this row.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
